Package: poulsbo-sgx-modules
Version: 1.0.0
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: i386
Depends: kmod, initramfs-tools
Recommends: poulsbo-sgx-userspace
Conflicts: gma500-blt
Maintainer: Poulsbo project <marcinkeviciusjustinas@gmail.com>
Description: Poulsbo SGX535 kernel driver stack (prebuilt for 5.4.0-150-generic)
 Prebuilt kernel modules for the Intel GMA500 / Poulsbo (PowerVR SGX535):
 pvrsrvkm (SGX render core, ported to kernel 5.4), a gma500_gfx that adds the
 PVR-over-DRM bridge and the SGX interrupt forwarder, and gma500dc (display-class
 device backing the zero-copy page-flip present).
 .
 The stock gma500_gfx is blacklisted and this stack is loaded by a systemd unit
 at boot in the correct order.  Together with poulsbo-sgx-userspace this gives
 accelerated 2D and OpenGL ES on the SGX535 under X11.
 .
 These modules are compiled for the 5.4.0-150-generic (i686) kernel.  Installing
 them on a different kernel will not load; rebuild from the project sources.
